        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This adds the <code class=\"notranslate\">permissions-policy-violation</code> report type to the <code class=\"notranslate\">ReportingObserver()</code> constructor. I've verified it works on Chrome as an observer and a server endpoint in the latest versions.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5105435227455488\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5105435227455488</a> says it was added in Chrome 120. I have verified this by running the <a href=\"https://wpt.live/permissions-policy/reporting/midi-report-only.https.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.live/permissions-policy/reporting/midi-report-only.https.html</a> test - which works in that version and later, but not before.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">WPT dashboard indicates not support in FF and macOS (which matches my testing): <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/permissions-policy/reporting?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/permissions-policy/reporting?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4260390029\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43783\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43783/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43783\">mdn/content#43783</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29500",
