            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Move <code class=\"notranslate\">revert-rule</code> from <code class=\"notranslate\">css.properties.all</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">css.types.global_keywords</code>, consistent with how all other CSS-wide keywords (<code class=\"notranslate\">initial</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">inherit</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">revert</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">revert-layer</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">unset</code>) are tracked.</li>\n<li>Add <code class=\"notranslate\">mdn_url</code> pointing to the new MDN documentation page (WIP).</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Support data unchanged: Firefox 150, Safari TP</li>\n<li>Spec: <a href=\"https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-5/#revert-rule-keyword\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://drafts.csswg.org/css-cascade-5/#revert-rule-keyword</a></li>\n<li>Bugzilla: <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2017307\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2017307</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Part of the <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4127711554\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43552\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43552/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43552\">mdn/content#43552</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29489",
            "title": "Move revert-rule from css.properties.all to css.types.global_keywords",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-15T14:42:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-15T14:40:39.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pepelsbey",
                "url": "https://github.com/pepelsbey"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds an entry for <code class=\"notranslate\">position-anchor: normal</code>, even though it's not implemented anywhere yet.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Ordinarily, I would not track something that does not have an implementation. However, it makes the existing notes difficult to understand, citing behaviors that were, at one time, standard but are no longer. Since there's no consensus implementation, I think it's easier to understand what's going on here with these changes.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">While I was here, I corrected the data for Chrome's initial value and note for Safari. I had previously erred in writing the notes in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4083024202\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29272\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29272/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29272\">#29272</a>. To \"test\" the initial value, I used the browsers' dev tools to inspect the computed value on an unstyled element.</p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3647585549\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/3558\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/3558/hovercard?comment_id=4171684032&amp;comment_type=issue_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/web-platform-dx/web-features/issues/3558#issuecomment-4171684032\">web-platform-dx/web-features#3558 (comment)</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2030351\" rel=\"nofollow\">Firefox bug 2030351 — Implement position-anchor: normal</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=311941\" rel=\"nofollow\">WebKit bug 311941 — Implement <code class=\"notranslate\">position-anchor: normal</code></a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://issues.chromium.org/issues/501399489\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chromium bug 501399489 — [css-anchor-position-1] Implement <code class=\"notranslate\">position-anchor: normal</code> </a></li>\n</ul>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29483",
            "title": "Add `position-anchor: normal`",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-15T08:05:56.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-14T16:34:28.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ddbeck",
                "url": "https://github.com/ddbeck"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/286386?u=bc4894b945491e0834d2306dade7fef748ddf698&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Added accepts <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;image&gt;</code> for <code class=\"notranslate\">light-dark()</code> color function</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Tested using these WPTs:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"http://wpt.live/css/css-values/attr-namespace-case-sensitivity.xhtml\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://wpt.live/css/css-values/attr-namespace-case-sensitivity.xhtml</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://wpt.live/css/css-values/attr-namespace-non-existing.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://wpt.live/css/css-values/attr-namespace-non-existing.html</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://wpt.live/css/css-values/attr-namespace-valid.xhtml\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://wpt.live/css/css-values/attr-namespace-valid.xhtml</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"http://wpt.live/css/css-values/attr-namespace-wildcard.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://wpt.live/css/css-values/attr-namespace-wildcard.html</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h5 dir=\"auto\">Passes With flag set <code class=\"notranslate\">layout.css.attr.enabled</code></h5>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Firefox Beta 150</li>\n<li>Firefox Developer Edition 150</li>\n<li>Firefox Nightly 151</li>\n</ul>\n<h5 dir=\"auto\">Fails</h5>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Firefox 149</li>\n<li>Chrome Canary 148</li>\n<li>Chrome Developer 148</li>\n<li>Chrome Beta 147</li>\n<li>Edge Canary 148</li>\n<li>Edge Dev 148</li>\n<li>Edge Beta 147</li>\n<li>Opera Developer 147</li>\n<li>Safari Technology Preview 240</li>\n<li>Safari 26.4</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43788\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43788/hovercard\">Content PR</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43789\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43789/hovercard\">FF release PR</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29482",
            "title": "added data for namespaced attributes in attr",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-15T10:01:41.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-14T15:52:27.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "dletorey",
                "url": "https://github.com/dletorey"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 145 adds support for the Crash Reporting API; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/6228675846209536\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6228675846209536</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Most of the BCD for this API has already been added; however, I wanted to add a data point for the <code class=\"notranslate\">crash</code> report type. The data for the different report types is contained under api.ReportingObserver.ReportingObserver.options_parameter.types_property, so I added it under there. This data is also used as the BCD for each report type dictionary; I'll need it when documenting <a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/crash-reporting/#dictdef-crashreportbody\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">CrashReportBody</code></a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is a bit weird, as <code class=\"notranslate\">crash</code> reports aren't observed by reporting observers, but I think you can still specify them as a valid report type in the constructor <code class=\"notranslate\">types</code> list.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29475",
            "title": "Chrome 145 Crashing reporting, crash report type",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-14T08:27:54.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-14T08:26:48.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7944955?u=2561481b8ea6df6246494193d1a08e1d44386ac0&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome is shipping the Prompt API in 148. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5134603979063296\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5134603979063296</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I generated a schema from existing BCD and tested the JSON against the schema.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29473.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4257144079\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29473\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29473/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29473\">#29473</a> and <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4249385804\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43755\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43755/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43755\">mdn/content#43755</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29474",
            "title": "Chrome added Prompt API in 148 #29473",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-17T08:01:38.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T18:54:49.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "jmedley",
                "url": "https://github.com/jmedley"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 146 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">TRANSIENT_ATTACHMENT</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">GPUTextureUsage</code>; see <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5562829589577728\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5562829589577728</a>, and also see <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-146#transient_attachments\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.chrome.com/blog/new-in-webgpu-146#transient_attachments</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds data points for the <code class=\"notranslate\">TRANSIENT_ATTACHMENT</code> in the places in which it appears.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29470",
            "title": "Chrome 146 WebGPU texture transient_attachment usage",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-13T15:48:02.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T15:44:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 146 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">texture_and_sampler_let</code> WGSL feature/extension. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5102334940151808\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5102334940151808</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds a data point for the new extension.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29469",
            "title": "Document texture_and_sampler_let WGSL feature",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-13T14:39:15.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T14:38:37.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">All SVG2 links in MDN are outdated.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Currently all SVG2 specification references link to<br>\n<a href=\"https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://svgwg.org/svg2-draft/</a><br>\nThey need to be changed to<br>\n<a href=\"https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/svg2-draft/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://w3c.github.io/svgwg/svg2-draft/</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4211836844\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43676\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43676/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43676\">mdn/content#43676</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29466",
            "title": "Update SVG2 draft spec_url domain",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-13T12:27:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T09:56:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Elchi3",
                "url": "https://github.com/Elchi3"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF150 adds support for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/script/type/importmap#merging_multiple_import_maps\" rel=\"nofollow\">multiple import maps</a> behind a pref (<code class=\"notranslate\">dom.multiple_import_maps.enabled</code>) in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1916277\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1916277</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This updates the feature.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4127672727\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43551\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43551/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43551\">mdn/content#43551</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29464",
            "title": "FF150 JavaScript multiple import maps behind pref",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-13T06:08:13.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-13T06:07:42.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80624252?u=abb5f45720c0c7db48614fa1cfe4ed7032af0a36&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Sets Safari's support for <code class=\"notranslate\">AuthenticatorAttestationResponse.getPublicKey()</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">partial</code>. The <a href=\"https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/#sctn-public-key-easy\" rel=\"nofollow\">Web Authentication API specification</a> (since level 2 where it was first described in) states that user agents MUST support algorithm -7 (ES256), -8 (Ed25519), and -257 (RS256). However, WebKit only supports -7 (ES256) and returns <code class=\"notranslate\">null</code> for the other 2 algorithms.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/52dbebe20b922cab89928085f9dcfa8082a813e4/Source/WebCore/Modules/webauthn/AuthenticatorAttestationResponse.cpp#L162\">WebKit source code</a></li>\n<li>Tested on Safari 18.6 on macOS.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29458",
            "title": "Update `AuthenticatorAttestationResponse.getPublicKey()` support status for Safari",
            "date_modified": "2026-04-12T23:41:37.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-04-12T23:40:59.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "pilcrowonpaper",
                "url": "https://github.com/pilcrowonpaper"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/118266?u=5a7fb2f3d1ecc7dcd73f43f4b478cb4938e6572c&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds relevant BCD for the <code class=\"notranslate\">shadowrootslotassignment</code> attribute.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://groups.google.com/a/mozilla.org/g/dev-platform/c/8qxAHE9-Xdo\" rel=\"nofollow\">groups.google.com/a/mozilla.org/g/dev-platform/c/8qxAHE9-Xdo</a> is my intent to ship this in Firefox. It is currently in Nightly behind a flag.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Refs <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4247443982\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43753\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43753/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43753\">mdn/content#43753</a>, <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4083478419\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12267\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/12267/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12267\">whatwg/html#12267</a></p>\n",
